     "page": 1,
     "text": "Printed by: ROI_60 11/10/2026\nCONFIDENTIAL - Contains PHI\nAdams Sanders and Wright Clinic | Dr. Kevin Cole, cardiology\nPatient: Donna Gross DOB: 01/02/1978 Sex: F MRN: 553088\n\n---\n\n**PROBLEM LIST**\n\n- Aortic valve disease (kind other; severity grade severe; repaired years 0.6) [controlled] onset 04/2012\n\n**MEDICATIONS**\n\nCurrently, the patient is not on any medications for her aortic valve disease.\n\n---\n\n**ENCOUNTERS**\n\n---\n\n**06/04/2025 Office Visit**\n\n**S:** The patient presents today for a follow-up on her previously noted ankle sprain. She reports that the pain has slightly improved but still experiences some discomfort with prolonged standing and walking. There are no other complaints at this time.\n\n**O:** \n- **Vitals:** BP 114/69, HR 72, RR 16, Temp 98.6°F\n- **Weight:** 124 lb\n- **Physical Exam:** \n - **HEENT:** Normocephalic, atraumatic. Pupils equal, round, reactive to light. Extraocular movements intact. \n - **Neck:** Supple, no lymphadenopathy. \n - Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops. \n - **Respiratory:** Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezing, rales, or rhonchi. \n - **Abdomen:** Soft, non-tender, no hepatosplenomegaly. \n - **Extremities:** Ankle shows mild swelling and tenderness to palpation. No erythema or warmth noted. Full range of motion in all other joints.\n\n**A:** \n- Ankle sprain - fair control. The patient’s ankle sprain is showing gradual improvement but continues to cause some discomfort.\n\n**P:** \n- Continue current treatment with rest, ice, compression, and elevation. \n- Patient to avoid strenuous activities involving the ankle. \n- RTC in 3-6 months for re-evaluation or sooner if symptoms worsen.\n\n---\n\n**04/30/2024 Office Visit**\n\n**S:** The patient presents today with symptoms of an upper respiratory infection (URI), including cough, nasal congestion, and sore throat. She denies fever, chills, or shortness of breath. No other complaints noted.\n\n**O:** \n- **Vitals:** BP 128/73, HR 76, RR 18, Temp 98.8°F\n- **Weight:** 128 lb\n- **Physical Exam:** \n - **HEENT:** Normocephalic, atraumatic. Pupils equal, round, reactive to light. Extraocular movements intact. Nasal mucosa erythematous, throat erythematous without exudate. \n - **Neck:** Supple, no lymphadenopathy. \n - **Cardiovascular:** Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops. \n - **Respiratory:** Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezing, rales, or rhonchi. \n - **Abdomen:** Soft, non-tender, no hepatosplenomegaly. \n - **Extremities:** No edema, cyanosis, or clubbing.\n\n**A:** \n- URI - stable."
